    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d472">

                <pb facs="0644" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg538"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lincoln to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-01-17"><hi rendition="#italic">January 17, 1891</hi>.</date>
                        (Received January 27.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 387.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your instruction numbered 350,
                    of September 2 last, I have the honor to inclose herewith copies of a note which
                    I addressed to the foreign office relative to the claim of Mr. Webster against
                    the authorities of New Zealand, and of a communication in reply thereto which I
                    have just received from Her Majesty’s Government.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert T.
                    Lincoln</hi>.</signed></closer>



